{
  "_notes": "Vanilla 26.3 blocks' own routines, recorded by the asset generator's HatchingFixtures.java against a block view of the case's setup (air elsewhere). A case with place sets that state at the origin with every update, as /setblock does; a case with tick runs the origin's scheduled tick, as the level runs a tick that is due; any other case random-ticks the origin's state if its isRandomlyTicking holds. The random is a legacy random seeded with seed, as both the tick's random and the level's. The level's environment attributes are the dimension type's own attributes and its timelines (from the dimension type's timeline tag) on a clock at time; biomes and weather add no layer. draws lists each draw in order. writes are the block changes in order with their update flags; each runs the new state's onPlace as a chunk does, then with UPDATE_NEIGHBORS its neighbours' neighborChanged, then the neighbour shape updates it causes. scheduled lists the block and fluid ticks scheduled, with their delays, once for each block or fluid and position as the level schedules them. sounds, levelEvents and gameEvents are what the level was asked to play or emit, in order (sounds without their seed, which vanilla draws from another random). entities are the entities added, with their position, yaw, age, home and persistence. after holds the final state of every setup or written position. chances samples gameplay/turtle_egg_hatch_chance at the centre of block 0, 64, 0 for a dimension and a clock time.",
